---
title: Otho Ontology Agent Architecture
description: High-level architecture of the Otho ontology agentic workflow
---
flowchart TD
    subgraph User
        U1[User]
    end
    subgraph Data
        D1[Excel Dataset: OthoDataset.xlsx]
        D2[Input/Output OWL Files]
    end
    subgraph Core
        PM[PromptManager]
        LLM[Gemini LLM]
        OG[LangGraph Workflow]
        S[OntoAgentState]
        CQ[CompetencyQuestion/Story Models]
    end
    subgraph Reviewers
        OOPS[OopsPitfallReviewer]
        RDF[RDFSyntaxReviewer]
    end
    U1-- provides Story ID -->OG
    OG-- loads story & CQs -->D1
    OG-- manages state -->S
    OG-- uses models -->CQ
    OG-- uses prompts -->PM
    OG-- calls LLM for OWL gen -->LLM
    OG-- saves/loads OWL -->D2
    OG-- validates OWL -->OOPS
    OG-- validates syntax -->RDF
    OOPS-- returns validation -->OG
    RDF-- returns syntax result -->OG
    OG-- stores results -->D2
    U1-- receives results -->OG
    PM-- loads templates -->D1
    LLM-- uses prompts -->PM
    CQ-- loaded from -->D1
    style OG fill:#e0eaff,stroke:#0366d6,stroke-width:2px
    style LLM fill:#fff2cc,stroke:#e6b800,stroke-width:2px
    style OOPS fill:#ffe0e0,stroke:#d63333,stroke-width:2px
    style RDF fill:#e0ffe0,stroke:#33d633,stroke-width:2px
    style PM fill:#f0e0ff,stroke:#a633d6,stroke-width:2px
    style CQ fill:#e0f7fa,stroke:#0097a7,stroke-width:2px
    style S fill:#f5f5f5,stroke:#888,stroke-width:1px
    style D1 fill:#f9fbe7,stroke:#cddc39,stroke-width:2px
    style D2 fill:#f9fbe7,stroke:#cddc39,stroke-width:2px
    style U1 fill:#fff,stroke:#333,stroke-width:2px
